{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q138008008","formula":"C₁₃H₁₈F₃NO₂","hill":"C13H18F3NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"F":3.0,"H":18.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"4C-TFM"},"descriptions":{"en":"4C-TFM, also known as TFM-Ariadne or 4C-DOTFM, as well as 4-trifluoromethyl-2,5-dimethoxy-α-ethylphenethylamine, is a serotonin 5-HT2 receptor agonist of the phenethylamine, phenylisobutylamine, and 4C families related to Ariadne (4C-D). It is a close analogue of the psychedelic drugs 2C-TFM and DOTFM, with 2C-TFM having no substitution at the α carbon, DOTFM having an α-methyl group, and 4C-TFM having an α-ethyl group. The drug is a potent agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2A, 5-HT2B, and 5-HT2C receptors."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":167243550,"mass":277.28,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCC(CC1=CC(=C(C=C1OC)C(F)(F)F)OC)N","inchikey":"KJEMUKCPDLOVTI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[2,5-dimethoxy-4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]butan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"167243550","atoms":37,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.794,"y":-2.127,"z":-0.667,"el":"C"},{"x":2.607,"y":-1.038,"z":0.383,"el":"C"},{"x":2.542,"y":0.406,"z":-0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":1.357,"y":0.676,"z":-1.113,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.008,"y":0.532,"z":-0.468,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.788,"y":-0.605,"z":-0.755,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.045,"y":-0.786,"z":-0.171,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.541,"y":0.185,"z":0.708,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.764,"y":1.327,"z":0.992,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.506,"y":1.506,"z":0.413,"el":"C"},{"x":0.305,"y":2.588,"z":0.628,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.131,"y":3.565,"z":1.564,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.896,"y":0.017,"z":1.349,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.916,"y":-0.047,"z":0.447,"el":"F"},{"x":-4.222,"y":1.054,"z":2.179,"el":"F"},{"x":-3.994,"y":-1.1,"z":2.123,"el":"F"},{"x":-2.86,"y":-1.862,"z":-0.394,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.379